WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
Someone reads you a phone number.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.360
Just once.

3
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:06.060
You turn to grab a pen, and it's gone.

4
00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.530
Every digit.

5
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.480
Now a friend tells you a joke, once.

6
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.950
Years later, at a party,
you're still retelling it.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.210
You heard both just once.

8
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.730
So why did your brain lose
the number and keep the joke?

9
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.430
Was the joke just louder?

10
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.900
Are jokes filed in a different place?

11
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.440
In this mission, you'll see how
memory takes information in,

12
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:32.040
keeps it and gets it back:
encoding, storage and retrieval.

13
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.990
And you'll meet three
ways to hold information:

14
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.450
as a sound, as an image, or as a meaning.

15
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain what your
brain did differently with the joke.
